# I-7 attribution — NOT node-failure data loss (evidence = mixed_load_bench.c seed code):
#   seed does catalogue_fdb_wipe() then session_put() x16 (clientid 5000+i) but NEVER client_put();
#   so the 16 0x70 sessions reference 0x73 client rows that were never created. I-7 therefore
#   fails on the bench-seeded keyspace INDEPENDENT of any node failure. This is a pre-existing
#   C-12 mixed_load_bench seed-completeness gap, surfaced here by running the validator on the
#   bench keyspace. No data loss: all real invariants (I-1/2/4/5/6/9) PASS and data sizes
#   3 MB / 637 MB are unchanged pre/post the failure.

=====================================================================
RESULT
=====================================================================
1. 1-of-3 node failure: cluster enters "recruiting_transaction_servers", available=false, and
   does NOT complete a recovery while the node stays down (>3 min observed, never recovered in
   that window). A minimal 3-node triple cluster is NOT continuously available at 2/3.
2. Node restored: cluster recovers to 3/3, available, replication Healthy, data intact
   (no loss; real invariants all PASS).
3. Implication (marked interpretation; mechanism = stuck TX-server recruitment at 2/3):
   production FDB HA needs more nodes / multi-region so the transaction-log group can re-form
   without the failed node. A 3-node footprint optimizes capacity, not availability-during-failure.
4. I-7 invariants FAIL is a SEPARATE pre-existing mixed_load_bench seed gap (sessions w/o clients),
   not a C-5 / data-loss event — to be fixed in the bench seed (follow-up, C-12 side).
